cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you reference this speculative model in your work, please cite it as
  a research artifact rather than as an established theoretical result.
  Principia Metaphysica is not peer-reviewed and is not scientifically
  validated.
title: >-
  Principia Metaphysica: A speculative G₂-manifold theoretical model
version: "2.2.0"
date-released: "2026-06-13"
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
  - family-names: Watts
    given-names: Andrew Keith
    affiliation: Independent researcher
repository-code: "https://github.com/andrewkwatts-maker/metaphysica"
repository-artifact: "https://github.com/andrewkwatts-maker/PrincipiaMetaphysica"
url: "https://www.xn--metaphysic-m6a.com"
abstract: >-
  Speculative model, not peer-reviewed. Principia Metaphysica is a
  candidate theoretical framework that proposes derivations for
  approximately 125 physical constants from the topological invariants
  of a G₂-holonomy manifold, anchored on the single seed b₃ = 24. Every
  model formula carries three independent representations (Arithma
  symbolic, EML compressed tree, Python float) cross-checked at
  registration. Predictions, closures, and compression ratios documented
  here are candidate proposals awaiting experimental confirmation and
  independent expert review; no claim in this artifact represents
  established scientific fact.
keywords:
  - theoretical physics
  - speculative model
  - G2 manifold
  - unified framework
  - unvalidated
  - candidate model
  - topology
